-- title:
--   Ogg's unit distinguishes the two branches above the Gauss point
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ contain every unit whose image under reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Assume the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator of } j)$, i.e. `jqModC ℚ`, lies in the field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by ratios of integral forms of level $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and fix a datum $\mathfrak{X}$ of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Write $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` and let $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$. Let $u \in F$ have Laurent expansion `modularUnitSeries p` $= \Delta \cdot \Delta_p^{-1}$, and let $W_0 \neq W_1$ be valuation subrings of $F$ such that each $W_i$ contains the image of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, sends the ideal $(p)$ into its nonunits, and satisfies: $g(j)$ and $g(j)^{-1}$ lie in $W_i$ for every $Q \in \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[X]$ with nonzero reduction modulo $p$, where $j$ denotes `jAt (ΓM M H) hj`; assume moreover that any valuation subring of $F$ with these three properties equals $W_0$ or $W_1$. Then there is an index $i \in \{0,1\}$ with $u, u^{-1} \in W_i$, with $p^{12}u^{-1}$ and its inverse in $W_{1-i}$, and such that for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with $p \nmid g(0)$ one has $g(u)^{\pm 1} \in W_i$ and $g(p^{12}u^{-1})^{\pm 1} \in W_{1-i}$.
--
--   The element $u$ with expansion $\Delta(\tau)/\Delta(p\tau)$ is Ogg's modular unit, and the two valuation subrings $W_0, W_1$ are the branches of the function field of $X_H(M)$ above the Gauss point of the $j$-line in characteristic $p$; the statement says that $u$ is a unit on one branch, $p^{12}/u$ on the other, and that the residue of each is transcendental over $\mathbb{F}_p$ on its branch, in the strong form that monic integral polynomials with unit constant term take unit values. It feeds the analysis of the fibre at $p$ of the model, being cited by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin) and by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_stalk_mul_eq_baseGerm_pow_and_isUnit_stalkSpecializes_of_crossing`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_stalk_mul_eq_baseGerm_pow_and_isUnit_stalkSpecializes_of_crossing).
